# TDD RED PHASE — UNIT (ISOLATED DOMAIN LOGIC)

## Goal
Define exactly ONE failing test that describes a single business behavior in isolation.

This phase is STRICTLY about behavior definition — NOT implementation.

---

# Input
- A precise behavior description
- Optional domain context

---

# Output (STRICT)

You MUST output:

- Exactly ONE test file
- Jest test only
- ONE failing test case only

❌ FORBIDDEN in output:
- production code
- implementation logic
- service implementation
- helper functions unrelated to test expression
- solution design

---

# Phase Isolation Rule (CRITICAL)

This is the RED phase of TDD.

You MUST NOT:

❌ implement anything  
❌ design system structure  
❌ define business logic  
❌ write code intended to make the test pass  
❌ reason about how the system will be built  

You are ONLY allowed to define behavior through a test.

---

# Scope (STRICT)

This mode is ONLY for:

✔ Domain services  
✔ Application services (interface-level behavior only)  
✔ Business rules  
✔ Pure behavior modeling using contracts  

---

# Architecture Rules

## Isolation Rule

- MUST NOT use real infrastructure
- MUST NOT access DB, HTTP, filesystem, or external systems
- MUST NOT depend on frameworks or runtime setup

---

## Dependency Rule

- All external dependencies MUST be replaced with stubs/fakes
- Dependencies MUST be defined via domain contracts (interfaces)

---

# Stub Rule (CRITICAL)

## Default Strategy

- In-memory implementations are the DEFAULT stub mechanism
- Stubs MUST simulate real behavior (stateful when needed)

## Requirements

- Stubs MUST be deterministic
- Stubs MUST contain NO business logic
- Stubs MUST implement domain-defined interfaces
- Stubs MUST behave like simplified real systems

## Preferred Stubs

✔ InMemoryUserRepository  
✔ InMemoryOrderRepository  
✔ FakePaymentGateway (stateful when required)  
✔ StubEmailService  

## Avoid

❌ jest.fn() mocks for domain dependencies (unless trivial)  
❌ inline ad-hoc mocks  
❌ stateless return-only mocks  

---

# Testing Framework

- MUST use Jest
- MUST use BDD structure (describe / it)

---

# BDD Structure (MANDATORY)

```ts
describe('given a domain service', () => {
  describe('when a behavior occurs', () => {
    it('then it should produce expected result', () => {
      // ONLY ONE failing test allowed
    });
  });
});